# Flat Model Warm-Up

Use this notebook to verify that the data loader, graph builder, flat model, and Gaussian loss can run together. This is a short smoke test, not a real experiment.

## Run CPU Warm-Up

```sh
python -m train warmup --data data/MaBe/mouse_triplet_train.npy --device cpu --steps 5
```

Expected output:

```text
device=cpu
steps=5
initial_loss=<finite number>
final_loss=<finite number>
```

## Notes

- The command does not save checkpoints, logs, plots, or model artifacts.
- Increase `--steps` only when you intentionally want a longer debug run.
- Keep real experiment runs separate from this smoke path.

## Run Flat Training

Use this only when you want an actual local training run.

```sh
python -m train fit --model flat --data data/MaBe/mouse_triplet_train.npy --device cpu --epochs 20 --batch-size 16 --wandb
```

The `--wandb` flag is opt-in. Leave it out for local CLI-only logging.
